data: {"chips": ["Story: Murders at Karlov Manor", "Play style: synergy"], "intro": "Recommendations grouped by how they support a Murders at Karlov Manor investigation deck: cards that bolster the investigators and value engines, cards that represent or exploit the murder suspects and threats, and cards that provide combat finishers and global effects tied to the set's themes.", "groups": [{"title": "Investigators & clue engines", "explanation": "These cards generate, use, or copy Clues and investigations, or otherwise support the deck's detective theme by converting clues and death triggers into card advantage and board tools.", "cards": [{"name": "Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/4/1/41129b44-4fa7-473b-b2b7-48c6a58be03c.jpg?1783912857", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/mkm/185/alquist-proft-master-sleuth?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature"], "color_identity": ["W", "U"], "evidence": ["lore"], "scores": {"story": 1.0, "synergy": 0.0, "similarity": 0.522, "total": 0.704}, "reason": "Alquist creates a Clue when entering and can spend Sacrificed Clues to draw cards and gain life, feeding investigation-based value and fueling further plays.", "source_urls": ["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-2-monsters-we-became", "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-6-explosions-of-genius", "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-8-gods-of-chaos"], "source_titles": ["Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 2: Monsters We Became", "Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 6: Explosions of Genius", "Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 8: Gods of Chaos"]}, {"name": "Ezrim, Agency Chief", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/9/5/9554d5f2-7a33-4734-8cf3-dfae2ccc3596.jpg?1783912850", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/mkm/202/ezrim-agency-chief?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature"], "color_identity": ["W", "U"], "evidence": ["lore"], "scores": {"story": 1.0, "synergy": 0.0, "similarity": 0.386, "total": 0.677}, "reason": "Ezrim investigates twice on entry, producing multiple Clues quickly; it can also sacrifice artifacts (including Clues) to grant key combat keywords, turning investigation value into protection or offense.", "source_urls": ["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-6-explosions-of-genius", "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-2-monsters-we-became"], "source_titles": ["Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 6: Explosions of Genius", "Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 2: Monsters We Became"]}, {"name": "Kellan, Inquisitive Prodigy // Tail the Suspect", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/c/4/c49690c7-c282-4eb4-8da3-5e0c46a80fc4.jpg?1783912845", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/mkm/212/kellan-inquisitive-prodigy-tail-the-suspect?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature", "Sorcery"], "color_identity": ["U", "G"], "evidence": ["lore"], "scores": {"story": 1.0, "synergy": 0.0, "similarity": 0.451, "total": 0.69}, "reason": "Kellan fits the theme mechanically and narratively: as a Murders at Karlov Manor card, it attacks with vigilance and produces disruptive value (artifact destruction and card draw) while its Adventure helps investigate and thin the deck.", "source_urls": ["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-2-monsters-we-became"], "source_titles": ["Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 2: Monsters We Became"]}, {"name": "Kellan Joins Up", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/2/e/2e7f95d5-b279-4469-9c89-1e02630d61e6.jpg?1783911793", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/otj/212/kellan-joins-up?utm_source=api", "types": ["Enchantment"], "color_identity": ["W", "U", "G"], "evidence": ["lore"], "scores": {"story": 0.0, "synergy": 0.0, "similarity": 0.515, "total": 0.503}, "reason": "Triggers on legendary creatures entering to grow the board and also plots a small card for later; it supports a legend-heavy investigator deck that repeatedly brings detectives or allies onto the battlefield.", "source_urls": [], "source_titles": []}]}, {"title": "Suspects, hunters, and lethal threats", "explanation": "Cards that represent dangerous suspects or provide assassination-style effects and face-down/assassin synergies\u2014useful for thematic removal, surprise attacks, and capitalizing on combat damage triggers common to the storyline.", "cards": [{"name": "Etrata, Deadly Fugitive", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/4/4/4410db5a-62af-43ac-979d-88a7c975f7bd.jpg?1783912850", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/mkm/200/etrata-deadly-fugitive?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature"], "color_identity": ["U", "B"], "evidence": ["lore"], "scores": {"story": 1.0, "synergy": 0.0, "similarity": 0.609, "total": 0.722}, "reason": "Etrata provides deathtouch and face-down mechanics that let creatures be concealed then flipped; she also has an ability that interacts when Assassins deal combat damage to opponents, fitting the suspect/assassin motif present in the Manor story.", "source_urls": ["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-2-monsters-we-became", "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-5-chains-of-expectation", "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-9-beauty-in-destruction"], "source_titles": ["Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 2: Monsters We Became", "Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 5: Chains of Expectation", "Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 9: Beauty in Destruction"]}, {"name": "Etrata, the Silencer", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/f/a/fa36b142-e67e-49da-9080-c5994e275266.jpg?1783934135", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/grn/170/etrata-the-silencer?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature"], "color_identity": ["U", "B"], "evidence": ["lore", "synergy"], "scores": {"story": 0.0, "synergy": 0.712, "similarity": 0.133, "total": 0.996}, "reason": "Etrata can't be blocked and exiles opposing creatures when she deals combat damage; that exile-based removal and the library shuffle/replacement effect make her a potent, story-appropriate threat to close out games and simulate targeted eliminations.", "source_urls": ["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-2-monsters-we-became", "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/episode-3-shadows-of-regret"], "source_titles": ["Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 2: Monsters We Became", "Murders at Karlov Manor | Episode 3: Shadows of Regret"]}, {"name": "Desmond Miles", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/c/9/c9523cd1-c3cf-4745-af09-77c1a83ac86f.jpg?1783910981", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/acr/24/desmond-miles?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature"], "color_identity": ["B"], "evidence": ["synergy"], "scores": {"story": 0.0, "synergy": 1.0, "similarity": 0.702, "total": 0.94}, "reason": "Desmond scales with other Assassins and Assassin cards in graveyards and surveils when dealing combat damage, offering a self-reinforcing Assassin package that pairs well with Etrata and other sacrifice/recursion themes.", "source_urls": [], "source_titles": []}, {"name": "Jacob Frye", "image_url": "https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/2/3/23422e75-e1c7-484b-aa1f-155ef9a998ec.jpg?1783910980", "scryfall_url": "https://scryfall.com/card/acr/27/jacob-frye?utm_source=api", "types": ["Creature"], "color_identity": ["B"], "evidence": ["synergy"], "scores": {"story": 0.0, "synergy": 0.789, "similarity": 0.773, "total": 0.785}, "reason": "Jacob's partner mechanic and trigger that can exile Assassin cards from the graveyard on Assassin combat damage supports an assassin-based midrange plan and recursion of key pieces.", "source_urls": [], "source_titles": []}]}, {"title": "Combat finishers, extra combats, and wide aggression", "explanation": "These cards support extra-combat steps, anthem effects, or punish opponents when creatures enter\u2014useful for converting clue advantage into lethal pressure or for recrea